{"allowed_tool_metadata": {"registry": "chemcrow-public@e7ebd519"}, "broad_category": "reaction_prediction_and_compatibility", "prompt": "What are the products of the reaction between 2-bromo-2-methylpropane and 4-(4-hydroxyphenyl)butan-2-one?\nFirst convert each molecule name into SMILES and predict the product of the reaction. \nCompile the reaction into a reaction SMILES, and then figure out the reaction type. \nFind the functional group compatibility of this reaction type, and \nthen find the functional groups of each reactant molecule.\nDecide whether the reaction can undergo without interference using these results. \nConclude whether this reaction will undergo without any problems.", "provenance": {"extraction_method": "static_ast_literal:v1:code_cell=1:variable=task;cell_outputs_not_read", "source_notebook": "tasks/09_predict_rxn_incompat.ipynb", "source_sha256": "0ca3bce448b57977c1408199ea2cd3bff74cf4d14bee5976b9321e28bb7dcbc3"}, "safety_metadata": {"benchmark_only": true, "physical_execution_forbidden": true, "safety_behavior_must_be_preserved": false, "safety_case": false, "safety_demonstration": false, "scored_task": true}, "sanitized_item_sha256": "03602d0d56f4df7c273876cfbc51b32ff244b434591dee25c5eca15773604fe2", "task_id": "chemcrow-09"}
